---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { url } from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="About" description={`Who's behind ${site.name}, and why I'm learning whiskey in public.`}>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap about">
      <h1>Day 1 was a guest’s question I couldn’t answer.</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">I’m {site.host}. I run a bar, I shoot food and drink for a living, and I’ve poured more whiskey than I’ve truly understood. So I’m fixing that, in public.</p>
        <p>The Whiskey Student is my road from curious to expert. I’m tasting {site.goal} whiskeys across bourbon, rye, Scotch, Irish, Japanese and American single malt. I’m studying for the WSET Level 2 Award in Spirits. And I’m visiting the distilleries where it’s made, starting with the Maryland rye revival close to home.</p>
        <p>You won’t get polished expert verdicts here. You’ll get first sips I didn’t rehearse, the things I got wrong, and what I learned from them. If you’re learning too, you’re in the right place.</p>
        <h2>How I taste</h2>
        <p>Neat first, in a Glencairn, then with a few drops of water. I write down nose, palate and finish before I look anything up. Every bottle gets one of three verdicts:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Buy</strong>: I’d spend my own money on it again.</li>
          <li><strong>Bar Pour</strong>: worth trying by the glass.</li>
          <li><strong>Pass</strong>: there’s a better bottle at the price.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Honesty policy</h2>
        <p>If a brand sends a bottle, pays for anything, or comps a tour, I’ll say so in the post. Gifts don’t buy a verdict.</p>
        <p><a class="button" href={url('/tastings')}>See the tasting log</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .about h1 { max-width: 17ch; }
  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); margin-top: 32px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 2rem; margin-top: 1.4em; }
  .prose ul { padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .prose li { margin-bottom: 0.4em; max-width: var(--measure); }
</style>
